        #revision
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            Chow groups with modulus are a non-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+invariant"} homotopy invariant
            variant of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chow+groups"} Chow groups
          %p
            In the theory of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/motives"} motives
            one studies
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/affine+line"} A^1
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+invariant"} homotopy invariant
            phenomena, like
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+Chow+groups"} higher Chow groups
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/motivic+cohomology"} motivic cohomology
            and homotopy invariant
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+K-theory"} algebraic K-theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categories+of+motives"} categories of motives
            can be embedded into larger ones which also contain non-homotopy invariant phenomena, like (honest)
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+K-theory"} algebraic K-theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+Chow+groups"} higher Chow groups
            in these larger categories.
          %h2#see_also See also
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/motivic+cohomology"} motivic cohomology
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+Chow+groups"} higher Chow groups
